=== main.frg
#include <stdio>

void show(float f) {
    print(f);
}

int main(){
    int hits = 7;
    int shots = 2;
    float ratio = hits / shots;
    print(ratio);
    double d = 0;
    d = hits / shots;
    show(hits / shots);
    float scaled = hits / shots * 1.5;
    print(scaled);
    print(d);
    return 0;
}
=== output
3.0
3.0
4.5
3.0
=== warning
warning: this divides two whole numbers, so the decimals are cut off before it becomes a decimal number
main.frg:10:24
main.frg:13:14
main.frg:14:15
main.frg:15:25
hint: turn one side into a decimal number first, like float(hits) / shots
